36	| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The schema is the format HLR-1's events must conform to; the strategy states HLR-1 cannot ship before the schema is settled. The emission implementation builds against the schema artifact, so the edge is serial. |
37	| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 / shared config surface | The serving-side implementation defines the per-project audit enablement configuration surface (the flag the serving path honors). The Dashboard admin control builds against that surface; serializing avoids two epics independently building the same configuration contract. |
38	| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation is blocked by all Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Docs edges do not trigger priority inheritance. |
39	| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same as above. |
40	| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same as above; the admin enablement workflow documented must match the shipped Dashboard control. |
