63	1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements; the Affected Components section is a bare list without change descriptions or owner teams. Team assignments were derived from the architecture context owning teams (KServe → RHOAI Serving; Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard). Epic-level acceptance criteria below were derived from the HLR text.
64	2. **Priority inversion in the strategy (resolved).** HLR-4 is marked P2 yet gates HLR-1 (P0) — the strategy text itself notes HLR-1 cannot ship before the schema is settled. Resolved in decomposition via priority inheritance: the schema epic (E001) is promoted to P0. Human verification recommended that the P2 label on HLR-4 in the source strategy is intentional (e.g., schema completeness for future components is P2 while the subset needed for inference auditing is P0).
