12	## Problem Statement
13	
14	Financial-services customers cannot pass compliance reviews because inference
15	traffic on RHOAI leaves no audit trail: there is no record of who invoked which
16	model endpoint, when, and with what outcome. Auditors require tamper-evident,
17	structured audit events for every inference request. Without this, two
18	strategic renewals are at risk this fiscal year.
19	
20	## High-Level Requirements
21	
22	| ID | Priority | Requirement |
23	|-------|----------|-------------|
24	| HLR-1 | P0 | Every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an audit event capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status (not payloads). |
25	| HLR-2 | P0 | Audit events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics and are not lost on component restart. |
26	| HLR-3 | P1 | Administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard. |
27	| HLR-4 | P2 | A common audit event schema is defined and published so future components (pipelines, workbenches) emit compatible events. Note: the schema in this item is the format HLR-1's events must conform to — HLR-1 cannot ship before the schema is settled. |
28	| HLR-5 | P2 | Documentation covers enabling auditing and interpreting events. |
29	
30	## Affected Components
31	
32	- KServe
33	- Dashboard
34	
35	## Out of Scope
36	
37	- Auditing of non-inference traffic (pipeline runs, notebook activity) — future
38	  strategies will adopt the HLR-4 schema
39	- Long-term audit storage and retention tooling (customer-provided)
40	
41	## Open Questions
42	
43	None — the audit sink interface is the standard cluster logging forwarder.
44	"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9afc93a15dd3fe65","agent_id":"afa1b5c98a7d3d61c","session_id":"d6022463-8a3e-4324-87fa-8d8b07f9d29c","uuid":"8d9a0100-aa7f-4011-a073-74f0c738cb52","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:07:45.753Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a09044b6bf003f8b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9010 decomposition"}
