30	# Dashboard per-project inference auditing controls
31	
32	## Description
33	
34	This epic adds administrator-facing controls in the Dashboard to enable and disable inference auditing per project. Administrators manage the audit configuration through the existing Dashboard project administration surfaces; the serving side honors the configured state.
35	
36	## Scope
37	
38	- Add a per-project control (within existing Dashboard project settings/administration surfaces) for administrators to enable and disable inference auditing for that project.
39	- Persist the control state via the Dashboard's existing configuration mechanism (Kubernetes CRs / feature-flag configuration).
40	- Surface the current auditing state for a project in the Dashboard.
41	- Restrict the control to administrator access, consistent with existing Dashboard RBAC patterns.
42	
43	## Acceptance Criteria
44	
45	- An administrator can enable and disable inference auditing for a project from the Dashboard.
46	- The control's state is persisted and reflected accurately when the Dashboard is reloaded or revisited.
47	- The control is restricted to administrators; non-administrative project users cannot change the auditing state.
48	- When auditing is enabled for a project via the Dashboard, inference requests on that project's KServe endpoints produce audit events; when disabled, they do not.
49	- Build pipeline is green for the modified repository.
50	
51	## HLR Traceability
52	
53	- **HLR-3** (P1): Administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard.
